semantic_diff: >-
  Base: revision 18, digest
  sha256:98aa5b8253190ce86cfd8978ca6c8b8c9b62e2ae126d7eaf83c90feb233f19bb, verified
  intact with pave-init 2.8.1 record_revision.py (19 revision_log entries) on
  2026-10-20 before drafting (host clock 21:35Z at the draft). The user's word, read by
  the lead at 21:21Z, verbatim: "queue 19 w/ 4 folds". This revision folds three nodes
  into the node each one already fed, and declines the fourth fold with the reason.
  Nothing new is added - no node, outcome, check, evidence definition, role, state
  field or effect that revision 18 did not already carry; every rule a folded node
  held survives as a step, an activity or an effect clause of the surviving node, and
  the text that only restated the surviving node's own rule is cut.
  Counts (MEASURED by parsing both graphs): 21 nodes become 18; 68 edges become 61;
  68 outcomes become 61; 14 checks, 25 evidence definitions, 8 roles, 5 control nodes
  and 19 required state fields unchanged. Purpose, scope, principles, roles,
  control_nodes, write_limits, state and completion are byte-equal. 14 of the 18
  nodes are byte-equal (every node but prepare_host, execute_attempt_loop,
  measure_candidate and assemble_kickoff_contracts); 12 of 14 checks are byte-equal
  (measurer_not_adjudicator's question names one measurement node instead of two;
  procedures_smoke_verified's failure route moves to measure_candidate); 21 of 25
  evidence definitions are byte-equal (four produced_by lists name the surviving
  node). 54 of the 68 edges are byte-equal; 7 are removed, 1 is renamed and
  re-pointed, 6 change one endpoint or their check list. Lines: 2820 become 2738 (82
  fewer), 169,922 bytes become 167,295; 20 hunks, 225 lines added against 307
  removed; the 3100-line
  ceiling is untouched. Layer test (pave-spec 2.1, revision rule 9): nodes, outcomes
  and edges are removed and one outcome moves between nodes, so graph meaning moves
  and the kind is graph; no seat, model, effort or implementation changes.

  WHY FOLD, AND THE TEST THAT DECIDED EACH ONE. The spec's inverse one-agent test
  (9.12) asks, for an edge A then B, whether one bounded goal holds both as
  activities while it keeps the visible outcomes, the user's authority, a required
  reviewer's separation, a recovery route that branches between A and B, an
  irreversible side-effect boundary, and bounded-context feasibility. Three
  boundaries failed to earn their keep: every outcome of the folded node landed in
  the same successor (recovery), or the two nodes were one seat of one role with a
  loop between them that only re-dispatched the same seat (measurement), or the
  folded node's two outcomes were a go or a return around the node it fed, the
  pattern revision 18 already used for kernel reviews (route review). The fourth
  boundary kept its question (fold 4 below). The warning sign is 13's "ceremonial
  decomposition": every step became a node because that looked more organized.
  Cost per run (ESTIMATE, nothing added): fold 1 saves one seat dispatch and brief
  plus two edge traversals with their outcome rows per host fault, zero on a run with
  no fault; fold 2 saves one measurer dispatch and two traversals per campaign, and
  turns each procedure or reference defect from a re-dispatch into an in-seat repair;
  fold 3 saves one node traversal per run, the reviewer seat costing the same as
  before (one seat with two or more requested targets, none with one). No fold adds a
  seat, a round or a re-check.

  FOLD 1 - recover_leased_host becomes prepare_host's recovery mode. Before: a host
  fault from the venv build (prepare_host.host_faulted) or from an attempt
  (execute_attempt_loop.host_faulted) went to a separate implementer node whose two
  outcomes, host_restored and host_unrecoverable, both went back to prepare_host.
  After: prepare_host has three entry modes - full, recovery, probe-only - and the
  attempt loop's host_faulted enters it in recovery mode; a host-level build failure
  inside the node enters recovery mode directly, so prepare_host.host_faulted is gone
  (an outcome whose only edge led back to its own node). Kept, as the Recovery
  paragraph and a recovery-mode activity: the allowance of one successful recovery
  per host per campaign and the flap bound; one recovery per host at a time with the
  shared-lease wait (release open job leases, wait for the owner's record, re-verify,
  take the owner's result); identity re-verification before any state-changing
  action, a mismatch refusing to act; drain, service restart then reboot; the
  boot-identifier amendment through the queue tool before the host counts as
  restored; the post-recovery probe transcript deciding restored, never the
  recoverer's claim; the conditional decision tier with probe-only mode as the catch;
  lease release on unrecoverable and no_host_available when no replacement exists;
  never the compile cache as a remedy, never the GPU baseline, never a host the lease
  does not name, never a whole-host action while another campaign's job lease is
  open, never provisioning. Cut: the recovery node's restatement of the identity
  rule (now a pointer to the rule above it in the same purpose) and its separate
  out-of-scope list, merged. prepare_host's roles gain delegate_dispatcher because
  the recovery node carried it and a role list is per node; the role definition is
  untouched. Removed edges: venv_host_fault_to_recovery, restored_host_to_probe_only,
  unrecoverable_host_to_reacquisition; attempt_host_fault_to_recovery now ends at
  prepare_host with its rationale; hardware_attempt_log's producers lose the folded
  node; execute_attempt_loop's out-of-scope clause names host preparation's recovery
  mode. The boundary to execute_attempt_loop stays: its KEEP question is the
  irreversible serving launch and the two different budgets (venv recipe retries
  against the per-target count, serving attempts against the same count under the
  bring-up ladder), and its recovery route branches - host_ready goes forward,
  product_defect_found goes to scoping.

  FOLD 2 - prepare_measurements becomes the first two steps of measure_candidate.
  Before: one measurer seat built the procedures and captured the baseline
  (measurements_ready), a second measurer seat ran them, and procedure_defect_found
  and reference_defect_found re-dispatched the first seat. After: one measurer node,
  three steps in one seat in a fixed order - procedures, baseline, runs - with the
  defect repair as a return to the owning step inside the node. Kept verbatim or as a
  step: the comparator set frozen in the design record and never chosen or altered
  by the measurer; smoke verification end to end with the known-bad-input negative
  control; the read-only GPU baseline capture with the skew record or the justified
  skip; revision entries that version each implementation and name the comparisons
  a revision touches; re-capture of only the comparisons whose procedure changed;
  a procedure defect invalidating the reference captured with it and repaired first;
  the lead-run digest-equality check on re-entry, now generalized to every re-entry
  (it was written for the candidate_serving re-entries; the evidence_unstable and
  evidence_gap_found edges entered the runs node directly, which the merged node
  now states once for all five routes); the shared per-measurement repair budget at
  the layout reference's section 4.4, unchanged in magnitude, now covering the in-node
  repair as it covered the loop; the two permissions kept separate - smoke writes
  scratch on leased hosts, the baseline is read-only always, with the section 4.10
  pointer; the five procedures and baseline activities. Checks: comparators_preregistered
  stays on the candidate_serving edge, which now ends at measure_candidate;
  procedures_smoke_verified moves from the removed inner edge to the
  bundles_stable edge into adjudication, first in its list, with its failure route at
  measure_candidate - its question asks whether every smoke record precedes every
  measured run that cites its procedure revision, an ordering that is on disk at the
  exit and was never decidable before the runs existed; what reaches the adjudicator
  is gated exactly as before, and a measured run before its smoke record is now also
  a forbidden effect of the node. measurer_not_adjudicator's producer set covers any
  agent at any step of the one node - the same set it covered over two nodes.
  bundles_stable's required evidence gains measurement_procedure_record and
  baseline_reference_capture, so the evidence measurements_ready used to require is
  required at the one exit that remains (stronger at that edge, never weaker).
  procedure_unrealizable and baseline_unusable move to measure_candidate with their
  edges to rederive_approach re-sourced; procedure_unrealizable loses its lost-serving
  clause, which serving_exhausted now states for every step, both routes ending at
  re-derivation as before. Outcome precedence: serving_exhausted, procedure_unrealizable,
  baseline_unusable, declared_measurement_unproducible, bundles_stable. Removed edges:
  measurements_ready_to_candidate_runs, procedure_defect_to_preparation,
  reference_defect_to_preparation. measure_candidate's allowed effects gain the
  read-only baseline use the folded node had and its forbidden effects say read-only
  always instead of no action, because the folded node's capture step moved in; the
  measurer role's effects over the run are the same set as before. The boundary to
  adjudicate_results stays: its KEEP question is measurer_not_adjudicator.

  FOLD 3 - review_route_verdicts becomes the review step of assemble_kickoff_contracts.
  Before: cost_routes_and_rank_backlog.backlog_ranked went to a reviewer node whose
  verdicts_sound went on to the kickoff node and whose material_findings went back to
  costing. After: the kickoff node has two steps, review then contracts; a retained
  adversarial_reviewer seat, independent of the costing seat and retained across the
  re-costing rounds (spec 9.4), reviews the gap-scan and
  route-analysis verdicts against the same three inputs before gate 1 is presented;
  material_findings is the kickoff node's own outcome and still routes to costing;
  with one requested target the lead records the review as satisfied with no seat,
  the outcome row citing the costing record, and the user's election is the review -
  the rule revision 18 carried, verbatim in substance. contracts_ready's meaning now
  states the order: the gate presented after the review record stood. The node's
  roles gain adversarial_reviewer; it consumes the delta report and the intake
  preflight record the review read and produces adversarial_review_findings, which
  it no longer lists as consumed. Why this is the revision-18 kernel-review pattern
  and not a weakening: the reviewer is a separate seat inside the node that holds the
  gate it protects (spec 9.4, review placed where the work it has not seen stays
  small), the artifact it reviews is produced by another node and another role, and
  the lead's one-target no-seat rule was already prose in revision 18, so the
  structural guarantee for two or more targets is now the same prose plus the
  outcome meaning. What passes gate 1 does not change: kickoff_contract_approved and
  scheduling_holds_recorded are byte-equal, the contracts step text is byte-equal, the
  user sees the reviewed backlog in the same order as before. Edges: backlog_to_route_review
  is renamed backlog_to_kickoff and ends at the kickoff node; sound_verdicts_to_kickoff
  is removed; route_findings_to_recosting is re-sourced from the kickoff node's
  material_findings. The boundary to cost_routes_and_rank_backlog stays: its KEEP
  questions are the user's authority at gate 1 and the reviewer's independence from
  the costing seat.

  FOLD 4 - trace_target_delta into cost_routes_and_rank_backlog: NO CHANGE. PAVE
  expresses fan-out only as an edge destination (pave-yaml 12.2: to: fan_out,
  for_each; spec 5.5.2: the only legitimate way to reach several destinations;
  9.6: parallel work is not designed until its join is designed). trace_target_delta
  is instance_per requested_targets - one parallel run per target, re-fanned per
  deficient_targets - and cost_routes_and_rank_backlog is the one run-level join that
  judges every report and ranks across targets. One node cannot be both the
  per-target runs and their join; a fold would either serialize the trace inside one
  costing run, against the user's parallelism word of 19:09Z and spec 9.12's "parts
  can and should run in parallel", or make costing per target and lose the run-level
  ranking and the rule that the seat judging a report is never the seat that traced
  it. The brief allowed exactly this answer. User-only line 17 (the op inventory with
  its kernel-gap list at target_traced) is therefore byte-equal.

  REVISION-18 USER-ONLY LINES 1 TO 20, EACH PRESERVED (verified by the byte-equal node
  list above): lines 1 and 15 live in calibrate_hardware and preconditions_to_calibration,
  byte-equal; lines 2, 8 and 18 live in kickoff_contract_approved, byte-equal, and in
  the contracts step of the kickoff node, carried verbatim; line 3, 11r, 12 and 13 live
  in design_campaign, review_campaign_design, adjudicate_results and the principles,
  all byte-equal; lines 4r and 5 live in realize_increment and changeset_complete,
  byte-equal; lines 6 and 9 live in adjudicate_results, byte-equal; lines 7, 14 and 20
  live in review_pr_evidence, impl_commit_is_reviewed, prepare_pr and
  pr_evidence_package, byte-equal; line 10 lives in the principles, byte-equal; line 16
  (measure_candidate's served cap row write) is carried verbatim in the merged node's
  allowed effects and first activity; line 17 lives in trace_target_delta, byte-equal;
  line 19 lives in scope_next_increment, byte-equal. No line is reworded, narrowed or
  moved behind a weaker gate.

  USER-ONLY-CHANGES CHECK: pending. Two readings, both recorded. Against the list in
  pave-revisions.md rule 6 nothing is weakened. Root goal and acceptance -
  purpose and completion byte-equal. Allowed and forbidden effects - two nodes gain
  the effect clauses of the node folded into them (prepare_host the recovery actions
  and lease amendment; measure_candidate the read-only baseline use) and lose none;
  per role, over the run, the set of permitted and forbidden effects is the one
  revision 18 approved, so no actor may do anything it could not do before, and the
  forbidden list grows (a measured run before its smoke record; baseline read-only
  always). External access - unchanged. Public interfaces - entrypoints and control
  nodes byte-equal. Evidence and check strength - every check keeps its question's
  claim; one check moves to the one exit that remains and one outcome requires more
  evidence than before; no check or required evidence is dropped. State authority -
  state byte-equal. Budgets - the recovery allowance, the repair budget, the stop
  limits and the re-trace bound are unchanged in magnitude. Against the plan's own
  rule 6 (SKILL.md, approval: when_needed) the lead applies without a user gate only a
  proposal that adds no gate, changes no outcome or edge, and changes no declared
  meaning; this one removes seven outcomes and eight edges, adds one edge, changes
  six edges and rewrites five outcome meanings, so it went to the user as one batch
  at the final digest; the user's word is recorded verbatim in the approval field.
  The three lines put to the user: (a) host recovery becomes a mode of host
  preparation - the recovery node and its two outcomes are removed, the attempt
  loop's host fault enters host preparation directly, and the implementer seat that
  holds the lease runs the recovery under the same identity, allowance and
  shared-lease rules; (b) procedure building and the read-only baseline capture
  become the first two steps of the measuring node, run by one measurer seat - the
  preparation node and its ready outcome are removed, a procedure or reference
  defect is repaired inside the node under the same budget, and the smoke check
  moves to the exit edge into adjudication; (c) the route review becomes the first
  step of the kickoff node, by a reviewer seat independent of the costing seat - the
  review node is removed, material findings become the kickoff node's outcome routed
  to costing, and gate 1 is presented only after the review record stands.

  USAGE EVIDENCE: none for revision 18 (applied 2026-10-20 21:04Z, no run). The
  predecessor-run records (EVIDENCE_ARC.md, ASSESSMENT.md, GRAPH_MAP.md of
  2026-10-20) describe a run that did not traverse this graph, so no traversal or
